# Safehouse occupants: the house as it is now (fed, short, after a death). Voice: the Haven's.
# Nobody threatens anyone in a house. A short house jokes about the soup, never about who eats.

conv occupant.house.fed
for occupant
when house:fed & !house:died
topic "Ask how the house is doing."
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say "Fed, for once. Someone brought tins and someone else found a sack of potatoes in a shed. We're having both."
  say "The children are arguing about the potatoes. That's how you know it's a good week."
  > @tin "Leave a tin for the children." -> tin   cost item:food*1   do favor:haven+2; regard:thanks
  > @fine "Good to hear." -> hub

node tin
  say "That'll be fought over. Thank you. Really."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

conv occupant.house.short
for occupant
when house:short
topic "Ask how the house is doing."
prio ask
voice haven

node start
  say "Half portions since the truck didn't come. The children eat first. Don't tell the council head I said."
  say "The soup's mostly water. We've started calling it tea."
  > @give "Put two tins in the stores." -> given   cost item:food*2   do call:hand_in:2; regard:thanks; keep:house.tins@here
  > @what "What are you short of most?" -> what
  > @promise "I'll bring two tins. Two hours." -> promised   if !promise:house.tins@here   do promise:house.tins@here:2h
  > @sorry "I've nothing to give." -> nothing

node given
  say "That's two suppers for somebody. I won't say who."
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node what
  say "Anything in a tin. Bread doesn't last the walk. And somebody to fix the stove, but that's another story."
  > @give2 "Put two tins in the stores." -> given   cost item:food*2   do call:hand_in:2; regard:thanks; keep:house.tins@here
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node promised
  say "I'll tell the children. No, I won't. I'll tell them when the tins are on the shelf."
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node nothing
  say "Nobody has. Come back if that changes. We'll still be here, most likely."
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

conv occupant.house.grief
for occupant
when house:died
topic "Ask about the candle in the window."
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say "We lost someone. The council will read the name at supper."
  say "You can stay for it, if you want. You don't have to have known them."
  > @stay "I'll stay." -> stay
  > @leave "I'll leave you to it." -> leave

node stay
  say "Sit at the end. Hat off. Nobody eats before the name."
  do later:6h:house.stayed@here
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node leave
  say "Thank you for asking. Most people walk past the candle."
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

conv occupant.house.bear
for occupant
when !house:died
topic "Ask about the bear on the door."
prio flavour
voice haven

node start
  say "So nobody shoots through the door. It doesn't always work. It works more than it doesn't."
  say "The children touch it on the way out. For luck. Its nose is worn through."
  > @back7 "Something else." -> hub

conv occupant.house.candle
for occupant
when house:died
greet
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say "There's a candle in the window, and people are talking more quietly than usual."

# Deciding together (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Several players"): the bed by the stove. Only someone the
# house knows can answer for it; the others in the room hear it (public) and can Object or Stand with.
conv occupant.house.stove_bed
for occupant
when house:short & !house:died
topic "Ask who gets the bed by the stove."
prio world
voice haven
scene stove_bed speaker who tier:haven>=known

node start public
  jump decided -> settled
  say "There's one bed by the stove and three who want it. The old man, the girl with the cough, the new one who stood the gate."
  say "The council says whoever the house trusts can choose. That might be you. Everyone's listening, so choose kindly."
  > @old "The old man. He's cold all the time." -> chosen   do decide:old
  > @girl "The girl with the cough." -> chosen   do decide:girl
  > @gate "The one who stood the gate last night." -> chosen   do decide:gate
  > @vote "Put a hand up for the girl." -> hub   do sway:stove.girl
  > @notme "That's not mine to say." -> hub

node chosen public
  say "Then that's settled. Nobody's happy, which is how you know it's fair."
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node settled
  say "Somebody settled the bed by the stove already. Nobody argues about it now. Out loud."
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

# Promises and callbacks (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Promises and callbacks"): a promise is kept by doing it
# (keep:) or broken when its play runs out; the next greeting says which. Greets show once a life.
conv occupant.house.tins_kept
for occupant
when kept:house.tins@here
greet
once
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say "You're the one who brought the tins. The children asked if you're coming back. I said I'd ask."

conv occupant.house.tins_broken
for occupant
when broke:house.tins@here
greet
once
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say "You said you'd bring tins. I told the children. That part's on me, not you."

conv occupant.house.stayed
for occupant
when due:house.stayed@here & !house:died
greet
once
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say "You stayed for the name, the other night. People noticed. Nobody will say so, so I'm saying it."
